        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>parent_log_context_offset</name>
        <qualifiedname>AVClass::parent_log_context_offset</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Offset in the structure where a pointer to the parent context for logging is stored. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For example a decoder could pass its <ref refid="structAVCodecContext" kindref="compound">AVCodecContext</ref> to eval as such a parent context, which an <ref refid="group__lavu__log_1gabd386ffd4b27637cf34e98d5d1a6e8ae" kindref="member">av_log()</ref> implementation could then leverage to display the parent context.</para>
<para>When the pointer is NULL, or this offset is zero, the object is assumed to have no parent. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
